# Real Vector Database

A real vector database stores embeddings permanently and searches them efficiently.

The project now uses:

```text
PostgreSQL
Prisma
pgvector
```

This stores embeddings permanently and allows retrieval to continue after backend restart.

## What A Vector Database Stores

It stores:

```text
embedding vector
chunk text
document ID
metadata
page number
user or organization ID
team ID
access level
```

Example:

```js
{
  id: "chunk_001",
  vector: [0.12, -0.04, 0.88],
  text: "CX-MA-001 - Amina Morrison...",
  metadata: {
    documentId: "doc_001",
    page: 6,
    branch: "Morocco"
  }
}
```

